# 🧠 Knowledge Index Template

This repository acts as a **dynamic context hub** for AI-assisted workflows.
Each `.md` file contains verified references, trusted sources, and key notes on a specific topic.

---

## ⚙️ How to Use
- At the start of any ChatGPT or AI session, include:
  > "Use the context from my knowledge index at https://github.com/jcalderman/knowledge-index.01"

- To reference a specific file:
  > "Use the context from my Blender index at https://github.com/jcalderman/knowledge-index.01/blob/main/Blender-4.5-index.md"

---

## 🧩 Structure Rules
| Section | Purpose |
|----------|----------|
| **Primary Reference** | The most official or canonical resource |
| **Verified Sources** | Reputable tutorials, docs, or data links |
| **Notes** | Bullet-pointed summaries or unique insights |
| **Usage** | How to load this file into AI context |

---

✅ Keep links short, verified, and descriptive.  
✅ Avoid duplicate topics — instead, link between indexes.
✅ Include version numbers (e.g. Blender 4.5, Revit 2024).  
✅ Markdown only (no code dependencies).
